<item><title>Zambian graduate with disability lands job after approaching minister</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/zm/zambian-graduate-with-disability-lands-job-after-c5183c/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/zm/zambian-graduate-with-disability-lands-job-after-c5183c/</guid><category>Zambia</category><description>Blessings Mulumbu, a University of Zambia graduate who uses a wheelchair, stopped Community Development Minister Sheal Mulyata at a community inclusion conference.</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 06:50:21 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/zm.jpg" length="32768" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/zm.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Zambian hospital completes two kidney transplants and targets 50 a year</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/zm/zambian-hospital-completes-two-kidney-transplants-and-cbc500/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/zm/zambian-hospital-completes-two-kidney-transplants-and-cbc500/</guid><category>Zambia</category><description>A wife travelled with her husband from Copperbelt Province to Lusaka to donate a kidney, while a 56-year-old man received one from his son.</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 05:38:13 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/zm.jpg" length="32768" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/zm.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Zambia hands K2.8 million school buildings to Malundu pupils</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/zm/zambia-hands-k2-8-million-school-buildings-to-malundu-pupils-cea870/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/zm/zambia-hands-k2-8-million-school-buildings-to-malundu-pupils-cea870/</guid><category>Zambia</category><description>Until now, Malundu Community School&apos;s lessons were held under a tree and, at times, in neighbouring churches, district commissioner Joel Mboyoma said.</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 03:52:52 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/zm.jpg" length="32768" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/zm.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
